(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[9 1 "// The sys module (Python/sysmodule.c; PY5e): made once per interpreter on its first import (sysModule),"] [10 1 "// from the host's configuration (Configure: argv, the search path). sys.modules is the interpreter's"] [11 1 "// Modules, sys.stdout and sys.stderr write to its streams, sys.stdin reads the process's standard input."] [12 1 "// sys.implementation.name is \"arbace\" (PYS15 (a)): Lib/test's @cpython_only tests skip, as on PyPy."] [14 1 "// The host's configuration, set before a run (Configure)."] [20 1 "// Configure sets the next interpreters' sys.argv and sys.path (the script's directory first, then the"] [21 1 "// standard library's Lib), each list's items separated by NUL; bin/pyi's host calls it before RunModule"] [22 1 "// or Repl."] [44 1 "// sysVersion is sys.version: the language's version, then pyi's build in CPython's layout."] [47 1 "// textFile is a text stream of the process (sys.stdin, sys.stdout, sys.stderr): _io.TextIOWrapper's"] [48 1 "// interface over the interpreter's buffered streams. The rest of io is _pyio's (PY6)."] [62 1 "// processStdin is the process's standard input, buffered once for every interpreter."] [81 1 "// unsupportedOperation is io.UnsupportedOperation's stand-in until _pyio (PY6): a ValueError (its base, with OSError)."] [84 1 "// ioMethod is a built-in method of t (PY5c's AddMethod: the dictionary filled once str's hash is ready)."] [100 2 "// the standard streams' attributes (PY6b's request: doctest reads sys.stdout.encoding)"] [175 1 "// exactArgsSelf checks a method's call: self and n arguments, no keywords."] [196 1 "// sysModule is the interpreter's sys module, made on first use."] [242 25 "// types.SimpleNamespace (PY6b: FrozenImporter makes them)"] [244 54 "// pyi's own .pyc files (PY6b): __pycache__/NAME.arbace-314.pyc, its own magic number"] [249 2 "// sys.flags as python3 -s -P -B runs (the references'): a namespace standing in for the struct sequence"] [261 2 "// the struct sequences of numbers and threads, as namespaces of CPython 3.14's values (64-bit Linux)"] [292 2 "// sys.monitoring (PEP 669): the tools' registry and the events' numbers; no event is ever raised (pyi has no"] [293 2 "// instrumentation yet: the debugging family's)"] [426 5 "// traceback objects are PY5b's (a Traceback is not an Object yet)"] [476 2 "// the hooks and introspection the stdlib reads at import (PY6a: threading, test.support)"] [507 3 "// PY6b's request: dataclasses' slots=True (unittest.mock's) removes the class's __dict__ and"] [508 3 "// __weakref__ descriptors before it makes the new class (sysmodule.c's _clear_type_descriptors)"] [546 1 "// displayHook is sys.displayhook: None prints nothing; another value's repr is written to sys.stdout and"] [547 1 "// bound to builtins._ (the REPL's expression statements)."] [564 1 "// sysAttr is sys.NAME when the sys module exists and has it, else nil."] [572 1 "// writeTo writes s to a file object: the interpreter's stdout when f is nil or None, a textFile directly,"] [573 1 "// else f.write(s)."] [594 1 "// exactArgsN checks a function's call: n positional arguments, no keywords (CPython's messages)."] [608 1 "// cpythonSizeof is sys.getsizeof as CPython 3.14 answers it on a 64-bit build for the core immutable types"] [609 1 "// and the list and tuple (the list's allocation taken as its length), 0 for any other object (PY6b's"] [610 1 "// request: test_marshal sizes its big-memory tests by sys.getsizeof of an int at import)."] [649 1 "// versionInfoType is sys.version_info's struct sequence (PY6b's request: test_importlib reads its releaselevel):"] [650 1 "// a tuple with the fields' names."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[119 53] [137 30] [198 48] [264 13] [264 26] [350 20] [388 62] [394 62] [408 26] [415 54] [418 26] [424 26] [425 38] [436 51] [446 56] [452 43] [455 46] [467 7] [467 30] [481 35] [497 34] [509 68] [517 41] [557 63] [566 48] [582 28]]} (go/file "sys.go" :import